{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"When exclusions eliminate all chat candidates, the request fails with a generic message that hides the cause."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A queued chat can disclose its private conversation to a model whose origin was excluded while it waited for capacity."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A panel can refuse a review after selecting an excluded verifier even though an eligible verifier is available."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A resumed evaluation can consume time and model capacity before failing on an excluded model in its saved switch chain."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The failure message repeats identical origin-exclusion explanations without changing the routing outcome."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The uneven source line wrapping has no effect on the rendered Markdown or its meaning."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Startup accepts the excluded roster preference, but the reproduced routing uses an eligible alternative and reports the exclusion among skipped candidates."}]}